 ## Background
-*   **Origin**: Proposed by Wang et al. in "LangSplat: 3D Language Gaussian Splatting" (CVPR 2024) [S1].
-*   **History**: Builds on 3D Gaussian Splatting [Parent] and addresses limitations of NeRF-based language fields like LERF, which suffer from slow rendering and imprecise features [S1].
-*   **Usage**: Used for 3D open-vocabulary querying, 3D object localization, and 3D semantic segmentation [S1].
+LangSplat was introduced in 2024 by Wang et al. [S1]. It builds on the principles of 3D Gaussian Splatting and addresses limitations in NeRF-based language fields like LERF, which suffer from imprecise features and slow rendering [S1]. It incorporates hierarchical semantics from SAM and uses a scene-specific autoencoder to compress CLIP embeddings [S1].
 
